Your digital‑banking operations must be kept in continuous compliance with the following statutes, circulars and RBI instructions :

1. **Statutes** – the provisions (as amended) of the **Information Technology Act, 2000** and the **Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023**, together with any other applicable legal requirements [md_13059::p00026].

2. **Circulars on domestic money‑transfer** – the conditions laid down in the circular titled **“Domestic Money Transfer – Review of Framework” (dated 24 July 2024)** and the circular titled **“Domestic Money Transfer – Relaxations” (dated 05 October 2011)**, as issued and amended from time to time by the Department of Payment and Settlement Systems (DPSS), RBI [md_13059::p00026].

3. **RBI instructions and directions** –  
   * **Regional Rural Banks – Responsible Business Conduct Directions, 2025** [md_13059::p00026];  
   * **Accessibility Standards and Guidelines for Banking Sector** (notified by the Ministry of Finance on 02 February 2024) [md_13059::p00026];  
   * **FEMA 1999** and any applicable RBI instructions issued under it [md_13059::p00026];  
   * **Instructions issued by DPSS under the Payment and Settlement Systems (PSS) Act, 2007** [md_13059::p00026];  
   * **KYC/AML/CFT instructions and directions** issued and amended by the RBI [md_13059::p00026];  
   * **Regional Rural Banks – Branch Authorisation Directions, 2025** (relevant where third‑party products are displayed on digital channels) [md_13059::p00029].

4. **General requirement** – All banks offering digital‑banking services must continuously comply with the directions contained in Chapter IV of the Master Directions [md_13059::p00025] and with any RBI instructions that are amended from time to time [md_13059::p00029].

These are the statutes, circulars and RBI instructions that must be adhered to on an ongoing basis for your digital‑banking activities.
